      "message": "refactor: remove hardcoded treadmill template fallback\n\nTemplates are data — they live in Cosmos as cardio-template docs and are\nserved to everyone via the data source (live API when signed in, SQLite\nsnapshot for anonymous visitors). The static TREADMILL_TEMPLATES mirror in\ncardioTemplates.js was still hardcoded template data in git, which is the\nthing we were moving away from. Drop it entirely; the drawer now renders\nstrictly from fetchCardioTemplates(). cardioTemplates.js keeps only the pure\ninterval helpers (getTotalDuration, formatIntervalSummary).\n\nThe snapshot has been regenerated so anonymous visitors read the templates\nfrom the cardio_templates table (no fallback needed).",
